Distinguish local free fall from tidal gravitational structure (@physics-spacetime-equivalence: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Compare-weak-gravitational-clock-effects-with-orbital-motion.lingua#r_0085AC67472F44FE636C42D515") { r_002F361B1AE054B0044156D39E
The equality of inertial and gravitational mass is a physical premise supported by comparison experiments, not a cancellation that follows from using one symbol twice. If m_inertial ẍ=m_gravitational g, universality of free fall requires their ratio to be the same across test bodies under controlled conditions. Air drag, charge, spin and self-gravity can violate the simple test-body setup without refuting that principle. The common model uses equality with an agreed unit convention; it does not assert a current experimental precision without its source.

In a uniform Newtonian field g₀, write relative position ξ=x−R(t) for a freely falling reference trajectory R̈=g₀. A second freely falling body has ξ̈=0. For a spatially varying field, instead ξ̈=g(R+ξ)−g(R)=J_g(R)ξ+O(|ξ|²). Shared [Compose local maps and derive change along a path](../../mathematics/core/Compose-local-maps-and-derive-change-along-a-path.lingua#r_001110BBF317180AC63FAA5412) supplies this local linearization. Removing the common acceleration does not remove differences between nearby accelerations.

For g=−μx/r³, differentiating components yields J_ij=μ(3x_i x_j/r⁵−δ_ij/r³). Here δ_ij is 1 for equal indices and 0 otherwise. Along a radial separation its eigenvalue is +2μ/r³; along either transverse direction it is −μ/r³. Neighboring freely falling bodies stretch radially and converge transversely at this leading order. The trace is zero away from the point source, although the tidal matrix is not zero. The singular origin lies outside the calculation's domain.

The equivalence principle extends the local freely falling description to nongravitational laws, with special relativity as their local form. General relativity uses a spacetime metric, a position-dependent quadratic form for infinitesimal intervals, and geodesics for freely falling test bodies. Curvature measures the obstruction to extending one flat inertial description across a region; relative free-fall effects are one operational way to probe it. A curved coordinate grid in flat spacetime is not by itself curvature, and an accelerometer held above the ground measures support acceleration rather than the tidal matrix. A single clock-rate difference alone does not establish spacetime curvature: accelerated observers in flat spacetime can also compare unequal rates.

**Read and work:** [Local equivalence and tidal gravity with Einstein Online](../sources/Local-equivalence-and-tidal-gravity-with-Einstein-Online.lingua#r_009C1733C562E19E367FFDB22C) supplies inspected local and tidal explanations. Derive the matrix above and its three eigenvalues at (R,0,0). Compare a 1-unit radial separation with a 1-unit transverse separation at R much larger than 1. Explain why a small freely falling laboratory can neglect a tidal effect only relative to its duration, size and required accuracy. Full metric connections, curvature tensors, Einstein equations and their solutions belong to the major gravitational branch; this lesson supplies their physical questions, not a proof of those field equations.

